{"seq":18,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/hermes-opus-gbrain-open-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T19:09:38.174Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"7b37b22f8d44fbac13067b0cfd2129e4e5a57a410fe58c11b2226e07aacdee23","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through every note Moss wrote (the Moss digests in the team folders). Only two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers show up:\n\n1. #PD-4492: \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers at the Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk (Doors 14-18, 04:00 shift) weren't getting their SMS bay assignments. Support patched it the same evening and Thea confirmed the fix on 5 Oct. The note's action item was to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n\n2. #4419: \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it went to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nOne thing to check before you use #4419: Marcus's own note \"Q2 expansion wrap\" (14 Jul 2025) gives #4419 as a Gate 3 BOL printer lag issue instead. That's not one of Moss's notes, but the same number has two different descriptions, so it's worth confirming with support.\n\nMoss's other North notes (pipeline digest 9/14/25 and renewal check-in 3/23/26) have no Quarrendon ticket numbers. The Central handoffs digest lists #4409, #4412 and FR-882, but those are for Marrow accounts, not Quarrendon. There's no members/moss notes folder.","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"}}
